# Dependencies
node_modules/

# TypeScript compilation
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Config & Secrets
# Catch-all: .env.prod (referenced by docker-compose.prod.yml) was not covered
# by the previous explicit list, so a real production token could have been
# committed by accident. Everything is ignored except the checked-in template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Lockfiles (project uses pnpm — ignore alternatives)
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# System & Editors
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Generated
/src/generated/prisma
coverage/

# Local assistant / agent instruction files.
#
# Working notes for whatever editor or tooling a developer happens to use. They
# are personal to a checkout and must never reach a published branch. At least
# one of these conventionally records deployment details, so keeping the whole
# class untracked is a security measure rather than tidiness.
AGENTS.md
agents.md
CLAUDE.md
claude.md
GEMINI.md
gemini.md
.cursorrules
.cursor/
.aider*
.windsurfrules
/.claude
/.gemini
